From: Alejandro Hernandez <alejandro@enedino.org>
Subject: [PATCH] cross-build: protect glibc mutex __unused member

glibc 2.43 uses a member named __unused in struct __pthread_mutex_s.
FreeBSD's compatibility headers define __unused as an attribute, which
removes the member name and breaks C++ compilation of bootstrap dtc,
including the pthread mutex initializers in libstdc++.

Wrap bits/struct_mutex.h with the existing Linux __unused workaround.
Protecting the defining header covers inclusion through both sys/types.h
and pthread.h without changing the host mutex layout or disabling the
FreeBSD attribute for bootstrap sources.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/build/cross-build/include/linux/bits/struct_mutex.h
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause */
+#pragma once
+
+/* glibc 2.43 names a mutex member __unused. */
+#include "../__unused_workaround_start.h"
+#include_next <bits/struct_mutex.h>
+#include "../__unused_workaround_end.h"
